infographic sequence-snake-steps-underline-text
data
  title How sampling turns interrupts into a hot-path verdict
  desc Periodic interrupts pile into thousands of stacks; the most-sampled function is the CPU hog
  sequences
    - label Interrupt 100 times/sec
      desc A timer halts the program on a fixed cadence, whatever it is running
    - label Snapshot the call stack
      desc Record the chain from main down to the on-CPU leaf at that instant
    - label Accumulate over 30 s
      desc Snapshots pile up: a 30-second profile holds about 3,000 stacks
    - label Rank by frequency
      desc The function in the most snapshots burned the most CPU
    - label Draw the flame graph
      desc Counts become widths: the widest frame is the hot path
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6 #f59e0b #f43f5e
